WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.450
What breaks in production?

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.531
A rule with automated
isolation could contain a

3
00:00:04.531 --> 00:00:07.612
server or an emergency
account by query; it's held.

4
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:10.814
A rule enabled without a
test is silent or noisy;

5
00:00:10.814 --> 00:00:13.524
it's held unless its test passed this run.

6
00:00:13.524 --> 00:00:17.188
A rule made in the portal can't
be traced; it's an orphan.

7
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:19.998
A plan changed after
approval means the approver

8
00:00:19.998 --> 00:00:22.876
signed something else;
publishing checks the hash.

9
00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:27.875
A renamed column makes a rule stop
firing; the weekly test run catches it.

10
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:33.770
And if the API isn't available in GCC,
the portal path deploys the same files.
